      {
        "id": 53080,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-02-18T00:41:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We played against Dawn earlier using Fanatic, Ab'Zero, and Haka. I played Ab'Zero, thinking that he'd do pretty well against the fire/cold damage dished out by the various Citizens. We actually had a pretty easy time of it and kicked her arse without a huge amount of trouble (and in Rook City as well!). Towards the latter half of the game, Haka got out a Savage Mana and started eating Citizens. Dawn also flipped at one point prior to that but there were enough Citizens already in play that she just flipped straight back again without us having to deal with her being invulnerable for any length of time. After we won the game I was looking through the deck. The next two cards were both copies of Return with the Dawn. I'd somehow actually <span class=\"bbcode-i\">forgotten</span> about the Devastating Auroras, neither of which came out. It turned out that basically the Citizens took up the top half of the deck - I think the only non-Citizen card that came out in the entire game was a Healing Light, which came out on the first turn and so was wasted. The only Citizens who didn't manage to come out were Anvil and Dare - everyone else had their arses kicked. The starting pair were Truth and erm, Autumn I think. The one who destroys Ongoings (it's Summer or Autumn, but I think Summer is the one who does fire damage). Anyway, Fanatic started with an End of Days in hand and played that to nuke those two. The game didn't get much better for Dawn after that. Yay for an easy win :D.</p>",
